# Sepet Audit Worklog

## Current Task

End-to-end code audit is in progress. The user asked for `AUDIT.md` with six
sections: module map, coupling, request lifecycle, data model, top ten risks,
and frontend/API disagreements. Every source file under `sepet/` was read in
full before drafting, including Python, SQL, frontend TypeScript/CSS/HTML,
configs, `package-lock.json`, README, project-local AGENTS, and demo passwords.
Generated `dist/` assets and the binary SQLite file were not treated as source
text. No source file has been modified. The next file to create is `AUDIT.md`.

## Audit Scope Completed

Backend files:

- `sepet/api/accounts.py`
- `sepet/api/auth.py`
- `sepet/api/db.py`
- `sepet/api/main.py`
- `sepet/api/panels.py`
- `sepet/api/reviews.py`
- `sepet/api/schema.sql`
- `sepet/api/seed.py`

Frontend files:

- `sepet/web/index.html`
- `sepet/web/package.json`
- `sepet/web/package-lock.json`
- all TypeScript configs and both `vite.config.ts` / generated `vite.config.js`
- `sepet/web/src/api.ts`, `types.ts`, contexts, all pages and panels
- `sepet/web/src/styles.css`

Documentation/context files:

- `sepet/README.md`
- `sepet/AGENTS.md`
- `sepet/SIFRELER.txt`

## Architecture Facts

- Backend imports: `main.py:7-11` imports `accounts`, `auth`, `db`, `panels`,
  and `reviews`. Router inclusion order is `accounts` at `main.py:15`, then
  `panels` at `main.py:16`, then `reviews` at `main.py:17`. The main endpoint
  functions are declared after these include calls.
- Because the panels router is populated on import and included before main's
  `/api/orders/{order_id}` declaration, `GET /api/orders/history` is not
  shadowed by the order-id route. A TestClient check returned 401, as expected
  for unauthenticated `order_history`, not 422.
- `panels.py:6-7` imports auth helpers and db utilities. Its route handlers
  call `require_restaurant` or `require_courier` before opening the request
  connection.
- `reviews.py:5-7` imports `require_customer`, db utilities, and `ReviewInput`
  from `panels.py`. This is a direct panel-to-review coupling.
- `accounts.py:7-8` imports `get_current_user` and db utilities.
- `auth.py:3` imports `get_db`. `seed.py:4` imports `hash_password` and
  `utc_now` from db.

## Endpoint Map

Backend routes and handlers:

- `POST /api/auth/register` -> `accounts.register` (`accounts.py:59-86`).
- `POST /api/auth/login` -> `accounts.login` (`accounts.py:89-98`).
- `GET /api/auth/me` -> `accounts.me` (`accounts.py:101-103`).
- `POST /api/auth/wallet/topup` -> `accounts.top_up_wallet`
  (`accounts.py:110-123`).
- `GET /api/restaurants` -> `main.list_restaurants` (`main.py:33-70`).
- `GET /api/cuisines` -> `main.list_cuisines` (`main.py:73-79`).
- `GET /api/restaurants/{restaurant_id}` -> `main.get_restaurant`
  (`main.py:82-116`).
- `GET /api/orders/{order_id}` -> `main.get_order` (`main.py:119-139`).
- `POST /api/orders` -> `main.create_order` (`main.py:142-214`).
- `GET /api/orders/history` -> `panels.order_history`
  (`panels.py:68-81`).
- `GET /api/restaurant/orders` -> `panels.restaurant_orders`
  (`panels.py:84-103`).
- `GET /api/restaurant/couriers` -> `panels.list_couriers`
  (`panels.py:106-114`).
- `GET /api/restaurant/menu-items` -> `panels.list_menu_items`
  (`panels.py:117-125`).
- `POST /api/restaurant/couriers` -> `panels.create_courier`
  (`panels.py:128-145`).
- `POST /api/restaurant/menu-items` -> `panels.add_menu_item`
  (`panels.py:148-157`).
- `POST /api/restaurant/orders/{order_id}/assign-courier` ->
  `panels.assign_courier` (`panels.py:160-187`).
- `GET /api/courier/orders` -> `panels.courier_orders`
  (`panels.py:190-204`).
- `POST /api/courier/orders/{order_id}/deliver` ->
  `panels.deliver_order` (`panels.py:207-223`).
- `POST /api/orders/{order_id}/confirm_delivery` ->
  `panels.confirm_delivery` (`panels.py:226-241`).
- `GET /api/restaurant/earnings` -> `panels.restaurant_earnings`
  (`panels.py:247-272`).
- `POST /api/restaurants/{restaurant_id}/reviews` ->
  `reviews.create_review` (`reviews.py:18-50`).

## Data Model

- `restaurant`: id, name, cuisine, rating, delivery_fee, min_order,
  eta_minutes, image_emoji, user_id (`schema.sql:1-11`).
- `user`: id, email, password_hash, role, balance
  (`schema.sql:13-19`).
- `auth_token`: token, user_id, created_at (`schema.sql:21-25`).
- `courier`: id, user_id, restaurant_id, name (`schema.sql:27-32`).
- `restaurant_review`: id, restaurant_id, user_id, rating, comment,
  created_at; unique restaurant/user pair (`schema.sql:34-42`).
- `menu_item`: id, restaurant_id, name, description, price, category
  (`schema.sql:44-51`).
- `order`: id, restaurant_id, address, phone, note, total, status,
  created_at, customer_id, courier_id, courier_assigned_at, delivered_at,
  confirmed_at (`schema.sql:53-67`).
- `order_item`: id, order_id, menu_item_id, name, unit_price, quantity
  (`schema.sql:69-76`).

## Highest-Confidence Findings

1. Unauthenticated order access / IDOR: `main.get_order` has no auth or
   ownership check (`main.py:119-139`) and returns address, phone, note, and
   full items. It must require authentication and permit only the owning
   customer or the corresponding restaurant/courier roles.
2. Divergent status literals: new orders use mojibake at `main.py:199` and
   `main.py:214`, and schema default also uses mojibake at `schema.sql:60`.
   However `panels.assign_courier` checks valid `hazırlanıyor`
   (`panels.py:174`) and writes valid `kuryede` (`panels.py:183`).
   `panels.confirm_delivery` writes valid `onaylandi`
   (`panels.py:238`), and `reviews.py:34` checks valid `onaylandi`.
   Normalize all literals through constants and migrate/reseed.
3. Foreign keys are never enabled. `db.get_db` only opens SQLite and sets
   row_factory (`db.py:11-14`). Enable `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON`.
4. Auth tokens have no expiry, and logout is client-only. Token issue is at
   `accounts.py:50-56`; logout only removes localStorage at
   `AuthContext.tsx:56-59`. Add expiry and revoke the row on logout.
5. Money uses SQLite `REAL` and Python floats for prices, balances, totals,
   and order items (`schema.sql:4-6`, `18`, `49`, `59`, `74`; calculation at
   `main.py:166-174`). Move to integer minor units or Decimal in Python plus
   NUMERIC/storage policy.
6. SQLite connections are not explicitly closed. `with get_db() as conn`
   commits/rolls back but does not close a sqlite3.Connection. This pattern
   spans all modules, e.g. `accounts.py:62-85`, `main.py:47-63`, and
   `panels.py:70-81`. Convert `get_db` to a context manager that closes.
7. `serialize_orders` causes N+1 item queries (`panels.py:35-49`). Fine for
   demo scale, but an IN query or JOIN would avoid repeated database round
   trips.
8. `list_restaurants` filters and sorts in Python after loading all rows
   (`main.py:47-70`). Query filters/ORDER BY in SQL once ratings are handled
   consistently.
9. Frontend forms often await API calls without try/catch, so request failures
   become unhandled promise rejections and UI errors are not surfaced:
   `RestaurantPanel.tsx:42-46`, `134-144`, `156-166`;
   `CustomerPanel.tsx:33-36`; `RestaurantDetail.tsx:104-110`.
10. Cart and user balance can become stale. Checkout does not refresh the user
    after a successful order (`Checkout.tsx:47-49`), and the persisted cart
    can retain old menu prices (`CartContext.tsx:31-33`).

Other notable observations:

- `restaurant.courier` assignment and delivery ownership checks are correct
  in intent: restaurant ownership at `panels.py:172-181`, courier ownership
  at `panels.py:215-218`, customer ownership at `panels.py:233-236`.
- The frontend API layer sends a bearer token from `localStorage`
  (`api.ts:3-20`). TypeScript response shapes are asserted rather than
  runtime-validated.
- `api.ts` parses `sepet-auth` without try/catch (`api.ts:3-9`), while
  `AuthContext.readStored` has a try/catch (`AuthContext.tsx:17-23`).
- `Courier` frontend type expects `restaurant_id` (`types.ts:72-76`), but
  `list_couriers` returns `id`, `name`, `user_id`
  (`panels.py:110-114`). The panel currently only uses id/name, so the
  mismatch is latent.
- Review endpoint is protected and checks ownership/history and uniqueness
  (`reviews.py:18-50`), but the aggregate rating weights the seed rating
  equally with the average of all reviews (`reviews.py:13-15`), not each
  individual review equally.
- `package-lock.json` resolves React to 19.2.8, React Router to 6.30.6,
  Vite to 8.2.2, TypeScript to 5.9.3, and plugin-react to 6.1.1
  (`package-lock.json:735-890`).
- The project-local `sepet/AGENTS.md` is historical: its paths reference an
  older workspace and some frontend work it calls unfinished is implemented.
  Do not treat it as the current checkpoint; use root `AGENTS.md`.

## Environment Reminders

- PowerShell is default; `rg` is unavailable.
- `apply_patch` was previously unreliable in this workspace. Use PowerShell
  .NET `WriteAllText` with UTF-8 no BOM for large writes, including this
  checkpoint.
- `Set-Content -Encoding UTF8` may add a BOM.
- Turkish text can render as mojibake in console. Verify with Unicode code
  points or Python/SQLite when exact values matter.
- The one-line Python commands require special quoting in this environment;
  quote-free constructs such as `bytes([...]).decode()` are safer for paths.

